motions.motion_text:
WHEREAS the Canadian Register of Historic Places (“CRHP”) is a nationally significant heritage resource that provides public access to information on more than 13,500 recognized historic places across Canada;
WHEREAS the Government of Canada has indicated it will no longer operate the current CRHP platform, placing the future of the Register at risk;
WHEREAS the National Trust for Canada is a national charitable organization dedicated to the conservation and stewardship of Canada's historic places and is well positioned to assume responsibility for the continued operation and enhancement of the Canadian Register of Historic Places;
WHEREAS the National Trust for Canada has proposed to assume stewardship of the CRHP to ensure its continued preservation, modernization, and public accessibility;
THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED that the Committee recommend that Council endorse the continued preservation and public accessibility of the Canadian Register of Historic Places as a bilingual, pan-Canadian register of recognized historic places;
BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED that the Committee recommend that Council support the National Trust for Canada's proposal to assume stewardship of the Canadian Register of Historic Places;
BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED that the Committee recommend that Council authorize the Chair of the Built Heritage Committee to provide a letter on behalf of Council to the Minister of Environment and Climate Change Canada, expressing support for the National Trust for Canada's proposal to assume stewardship of the Canadian Register of Historic Places;
BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED that Built Heritage Committee submit this Motion for Council consideration at its meeting of July 15, 2026, so that the letter of support may be provided before the end of July.
